diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d04f33a..924988d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,8 +6,24 @@ Converts a transaction log to CSV for the reporting tools.
 cargo run -q < transactions.tsv > ledger.csv
 ```
 
-Input: one transaction per line, `date<TAB>account<TAB>amount` (ISO date,
-amount with up to two decimals). Blank lines and `#` comments are skipped.
+Input: one transaction per line, `date<TAB>account<TAB>amount[<TAB>currency]`
+(ISO date, amount with up to two decimals). Blank lines and `#` comments are
+skipped.
 
-Output: `date,account,amount_cents`. Any malformed line stops the export
-with `line N: ...` on stderr and exit status 1.
+The optional fourth column is the ISO 4217 currency code: exactly three
+uppercase ASCII letters, such as `EUR`. When the column is missing the currency
+is `USD`. Leading and trailing spaces around a column are ignored.
+
+Output: `date,account,amount_cents,currency`, with one row per input line and
+the currency on every row.
+
+Exit status:
+
+- `0`: success.
+- `1`: any malformed line other than a bad currency code (wrong field count,
+  bad date, bad account, bad amount). Stderr gets `line N: ...`.
+- `2`: a malformed currency code (for example `usd`, `US` or `USDX`). Stderr
+  gets `line N: bad currency ...`.
+
+The export stops at the first bad line, so the output is incomplete when the
+exit status is not `0`.
